---
title: "Conventional and Alternate Energy Applications"
code: "ENE-100"
category: "energy-technology"
credits: "4"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/ELE-176"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: ELE 176 or instructor approval."
---

Provides an overview of hydroelectric, coal, and nuclear energy production methods and renewable solar, geothermal, wind, and fuel cell technology. A complete system breakdown of conventional power production methods, efficiency, and sustainability when compared with solar. Lecture 3 hours. Laboratory 3 ours. Total 6 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
